---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SEOHead from '../components/SEOHead.astro';
import { url } from '../utils/paths';
---
<Base title="Fractional CMO and AI marketing services" description="You can work with Manual Focus as a strategic advisor, a fractional CMO or on a fixed-price build, or have us run your AI workflows through Manual Focus AI.">
  <SEOHead slot="seo" type="service" title="Fractional CMO and AI marketing services" description="You can work with Manual Focus as a strategic advisor, a fractional CMO or on a fixed-price build, or have us run your AI workflows through Manual Focus AI." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Services', url: '/services/' }]} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">SERVICES</div>
      <h1>How we work together</h1>
      <p class="lead">You can work with us in three ways, and each one builds AI into the workflows your team already runs. There's also a product, Manual Focus AI, where we run the workflows and deliver the output. Every engagement starts with a free 30-minute working session.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Strategic Advisor -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/01 · STRATEGIC ADVISOR</div>
        <h2>Your team ships work without anyone steering.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits companies with a marketing team but no senior leader running it.</p>
        <p>You have people doing the work but nobody senior to call the shots, review the output and ask the harder questions. We sit alongside the team for a handful of sessions a month, so you get a CMO's strategic input without the cost or commitment of hiring one.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Weekly or fortnightly working sessions on what to do next</li>
          <li>Reviews of campaigns, content and creative before they ship</li>
          <li>Quarterly planning and priority-setting with the team</li>
          <li>Briefings on the AI tooling and emerging tech worth using, and where it fits the workflows your team already runs</li>
          <li>Hiring and team-shape advice as you grow the function</li>
          <li>A direct line between sessions for the calls that won't wait</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What stays with your team</h3>
        <p>Your team keeps running itself and shipping the work, and we join a handful of meetings a month rather than all of them. If you want someone embedded in your leadership team, that's the Fractional CMO.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · 1–2 days a month, on a day rate or monthly retainer</p>
        <p class="service-proof">James works this way with companies that use AI to manage people's wealth.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=strategic-advisor`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fractional CMO -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/02 · FRACTIONAL CMO</div>
        <h2>You need a part-time CMO.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits companies that need senior marketing leadership without making a full-time hire.</p>
        <p>We join your leadership team, set the marketing thesis, build the plan, lead the people you already have and ship the pieces that need senior hands. We wire AI and emerging tech into the workflows your team already runs, so a small team gets through the work of a much larger one. You get a CMO's seniority for a fraction of the cost, and the work ships alongside the strategy.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Marketing thesis, 90-day plan and quarterly OKRs</li>
          <li>Leading and growing the existing team (or hiring it)</li>
          <li>Embedding AI and emerging tech into the workflows your team already runs, day by day</li>
          <li>Shipping key campaigns, launches and content with AI in place</li>
          <li>Owning reporting to the CEO and board</li>
          <li>Input into product, pricing and positioning decisions</li>
          <li>Shorter production cycles, using the Forge tooling</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What to expect</h3>
        <p>You get a senior marketer who ships the work as well as planning it. The seat is part-time by design, so we set the cadence to make the most of one or two days a week.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · 1–2 days a week, three-month minimum</p>
        <p class="service-proof">James led marketing from the inside at RGT Cycling, where he was on the founding team and took it from 19k to 350k users before Wahoo bought it. He has also led marketing for a privacy-focused crypto project worth $200M.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=fractional-cmo`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Build & Hand Over -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/03 · BUILD &amp; HAND OVER</div>
        <h2>You know what you need built.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits companies that want a specific piece of marketing shipped fast.</p>
        <p>You might want a launch, a website rebuild, an SEO programme, a brand refresh or a content engine. We build it end to end with AI and emerging tech wired in from the start, then hand it back to your team to run, with documentation and training to keep it going.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Product or feature launches, with positioning, narrative and assets</li>
          <li>Commerce rebuilds on Shopify, BigCommerce or WooCommerce/WordPress, full-stack or headless, shipped fast</li>
          <li>Headless web builds on composable stacks, made for speed, SEO and a clean handover</li>
          <li>Landing systems and conversion infrastructure (Next, Astro, Webflow where it fits)</li>
          <li>SEO and answer-engine optimisation programmes, including content engines</li>
          <li>Brand refreshes with messaging architecture and visual direction</li>
          <li>PR campaigns with journalist outreach, story arcs and placement</li>
          <li>AI and emerging-tech workflows built into your existing stack</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How it ends</h3>
        <p>We fix the scope and the price up front, and once the build ships we hand it over, so your team owns it from then on.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · Fixed scope, timeline and price, with most builds taking 4–12 weeks</p>
        <p class="service-proof">You can see the method on our own site in the <a href={url('/lens/ops/site-audit-and-refresh/')}>September 2026 audit and refresh</a>, with the retest logs published.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=build-and-hand-over`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- /04 Manual Focus AI · the product -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail service-detail-product reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/04 · MANUAL FOCUS · AI <span class="service-tag-flag">PRODUCT</span></div>
        <h2>You get the output of AI workflows we run for you.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits CTOs, CMOs and teams who can't find the time to keep up with new models, build pipelines or learn another tool every week.</p>
        <p>Manual Focus AI is the product side of the agency, where we run the workflows ourselves instead of teaching your team to. We do the content planning, wireframing and production on the Forge and deliver the output into your stack on an agreed schedule. When a better model ships, we swap it in, and all you notice is that the output keeps getting better.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Content planning pipelines for calendars, briefs, drafts and fact-checks</li>
          <li>Wireframes and creative production for landing pages, ad units and social packs</li>
          <li>A weekly digest of competitor moves, search ranking shifts and model launches</li>
          <li>Pipeline maintenance, re-tooled as new models and capabilities ship</li>
          <li>Output in your brand and your stack, ready to use</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What your team does</h3>
        <p>Your team has nobody to manage, no tool to learn and no training to sit through, because we run the workflows, tune them to your brand and priorities, and send the output on the agreed schedule.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · Monthly retainer, output on an agreed schedule, three-month minimum</p>
        <p class="service-proof">You can see it running in the <a href={url('/lens/content/news-desk/')}>news desk</a> behind our own AI briefing, which shortlists the day's stories and publishes only the ones that clear the bar.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=manual-focus-ai`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Specialism note -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">VERTICAL DEPTH</div>
      <h2 class="vertical-headline">Endurance and sports brands<br/>are where we've shipped the most.</h2>
      <p class="vertical-copy">If you're building in endurance, sports or the wider fitness category, you get a team that has run marketing in your category at scale. James Vickers, our founder, was on the founding team at RGT Cycling and took it from 19k to 350k users before Wahoo Fitness bought it. We've also led marketing in AI, fintech, hardware and digital assets, so the playbook travels. For search, read the <a href={url('/blog/seo-playbook-premium-endurance-brands/')}>SEO playbook for premium endurance brands</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">WHAT HAPPENS NEXT</div>
      <ol class="next-steps-list">
        <li><strong>We meet for a free 30-minute working session.</strong> You bring the problem, and we bring questions and a first view on it.</li>
        <li><strong>If it's a fit, you get a written scope.</strong> It sets out the shape of the engagement and the cost, and builds get a fixed price up front.</li>
        <li><strong>We start.</strong> On a Fractional CMO engagement, we set the thesis and a 90-day plan in the first month.</li>
      </ol>
      <a href={url('/enquire/')} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .service-detail {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
  }

  /* Product tier — distinct from the three engagement tiers above */
  .service-detail-product {
    position: relative;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(192, 38, 211, 0.05), rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.02)),
      var(--color-bg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .service-detail-product::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--color-cta-gradient);
  }
  .service-tag-flag {
    margin-left: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-cta-end);
    color: var(--color-cta-end);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    background: rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.06);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .service-detail-product { padding: var(--space-lg); }
  }

  .service-tag {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .service-for {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail > p {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .service-detail ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail ul li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .service-proof {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .service-proof a,
  .vertical-copy a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }

  .next-steps-list {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .next-steps-list strong { color: var(--color-text); }

  .service-shape {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .vertical-headline {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .vertical-copy {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
</style>
